-- title:
--   Crossings in the special fibre count supersingular places
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 5$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of type $\{p\}$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))/L$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb Q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and let $A$ act on $K$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ have image in $L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator of } j)$, and assume $j \neq 0$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral. Write $X_k = \operatorname{Spec} k \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} (\text{two-chart model } \mathrm{ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo}\ A\ K\ j)$ with its projection `baseChange` to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and let $i_1, i_2$ be morphisms $C_1 \to X_k$, $C_2 \to X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ (i.e. whose composites with that projection are $c_1$, $c_2$) which are closed immersions. Assume every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, that the scheme $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and that its underlying set has exactly $n$ points with $n > 0$. Finally let $\bar\jmath$ be an element of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134), the $k$-subfield of $k((q))$ of $q$-expansions for $\Gamma_1(M)$, whose image in $k((q))$ is [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), the mod-$p$ $j$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator of } j)$. Then $n$ equals the number of places $v$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) over $k$ — valuation subrings containing the image of $k$, proper, and principal ideal rings — such that $\bar\jmath$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$ and the residue $v.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\bar\jmath \in k$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p k`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $p$.
--
--   This is the numerical part of the Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur description of the special fibre of the stable model of $X_1(Mp)$ for $p \nmid M$: the two components meet transversally in exactly one point above each supersingular point of $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$, and the count of crossings is here identified with the number of supersingular places of the function field of $X_1(M)_k$. It is used downstream in the analysis of the torsion and of the Picard group pairing for the special fibre.
